1
00:00:10,670 --> 00:00:14,090
Marilyn, you want coffee or tea?

2
00:00:14,090 --> 00:00:28,800
Coffee, please.

3
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:31,150
I am so excited!

4
00:00:31,150 --> 00:00:32,630
At this time tomorrow morning,

5
00:00:32,630 --> 00:00:40,950
Grandpa will be sitting in the kitchen with us.

6
00:00:40,950 --> 00:00:42,590
When does he arrive?

7
00:00:42,590 --> 00:00:45,460
At six o'clock this evening.

8
00:00:45,460 --> 00:00:46,720
By plane?

9
00:00:46,720 --> 00:00:50,580
No, by train.

10
00:00:50,580 --> 00:00:53,030
Are we picking him up at the station?

11
00:00:53,030 --> 00:00:54,380
Not Grandpa.

12
00:00:54,380 --> 00:00:57,600
He doesn't want anybody picking him up.

13
00:00:57,600 --> 00:01:00,010
He likes to be independent.

14
00:01:00,010 --> 00:01:00,940
Huh.

15
00:01:00,940 --> 00:01:03,850
Oh, let's go upstairs and prepare Grandpa's room.

16
00:01:03,850 --> 00:01:07,340
Great! Let's do it!

17
00:01:07,340 --> 00:01:08,430
Good morning, Mom.

18
00:01:08,430 --> 00:01:09,220
Morning.

19
00:01:09,220 --> 00:01:09,720
Well, hi, fellas.

20
00:01:09,720 --> 00:01:10,330
Hello.

21
00:01:10,330 --> 00:01:10,670
Hi, honey.

22
00:01:10,670 --> 00:01:11,420
Morning, Marilyn.

23
00:01:11,420 --> 00:01:12,960
We are going upstairs to set up Grandpa's room.

24
00:01:12,960 --> 00:01:17,690
There's coffee ready.

25
00:01:17,690 --> 00:01:19,920
I'm really excited about seeing Grandpa.

26
00:01:19,920 --> 00:01:23,480
Me, too. Milk, please.

27
00:01:23,480 --> 00:01:24,640
He's so funny.

28
00:01:24,640 --> 00:01:28,650
He always makes me laugh.

29
00:01:28,650 --> 00:01:30,790
I hope Grandpa's going to like living with us.

30
00:01:30,790 --> 00:01:32,300
I think he will.

31
00:01:32,300 --> 00:01:34,730
It just takes time to feel comfortable in a new place.

32
00:01:34,730 --> 00:01:36,370
Won't he miss being in Florida?

33
00:01:36,370 --> 00:01:37,300
Well, he will.

34
00:01:37,300 --> 00:01:39,490
But I think he'll like being here with the family.

35
00:01:39,490 --> 00:01:40,780
Are you sure about that?

36
00:01:40,780 --> 00:01:42,440
It's crazy here most of the time.

37
00:01:42,440 --> 00:01:43,700
But it's fun.

38
00:01:43,700 --> 00:01:45,860
That's for sure.

39
00:01:45,860 --> 00:01:46,490
You know,

40
00:01:46,490 --> 00:01:48,850
maybe I'll put together some photos of Grandpa

41
00:01:48,850 --> 00:01:50,220
as a "welcome" present.

42
00:01:50,220 --> 00:01:52,280
That's a neat idea.

43
00:01:52,280 --> 00:01:53,990
What can I do?

44
00:01:53,990 --> 00:01:55,010
I've got it!

45
00:01:55,010 --> 00:01:59,640
I have a picture of Grandpa and Dad and me in my wallet.

46
00:01:59,640 --> 00:02:01,470
It's from the Fathers and Sons' Breakfast

47
00:02:01,470 --> 00:02:04,060
at my junior high school graduation.

48
00:02:04,060 --> 00:02:08,170
Oh, I remember this picture.

49
00:02:08,170 --> 00:02:11,600
I'd really like to pick up Grandpa at the railroad station.

50
00:02:11,600 --> 00:02:13,820
Railroad stations or airports.

51
00:02:13,820 --> 00:02:16,490
Grandpa always tells us he'll get here by himself.

52
00:02:16,490 --> 00:02:23,050
He's something!

53
00:02:23,050 --> 00:02:25,600
Is this all Grandpa's stuff?

54
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:26,920
That's it.

55
00:02:26,920 --> 00:02:31,490
But I'm sure he has a few bags with him on the train.

56
00:02:31,490 --> 00:02:34,890
What's inside?

57
00:02:34,890 --> 00:02:41,790
I don't know. It's locked.

58
00:02:41,790 --> 00:02:42,990
Hi.

59
00:02:42,990 --> 00:02:43,840
Oh, hi, darling.

60
00:02:43,840 --> 00:02:44,700
Morning, Philip.

61
00:02:44,700 --> 00:02:47,860
I want to put some of my good hangers in Grandpa's closet.

62
00:02:47,860 --> 00:02:51,190
You know I'm very excited about his arrival.

63
00:02:51,190 --> 00:02:53,110
We are, too.

64
00:02:53,110 --> 00:02:55,310
Susan called early this morning.

65
00:02:55,310 --> 00:02:56,190
She's unhappy

66
00:02:56,190 --> 00:02:59,410
because she's had to go to Chicago on a business trip

67
00:02:59,410 --> 00:03:01,020
and can't leave till tonight.

68
00:03:01,020 --> 00:03:02,880
She wants to be here for Grandpa.

69
00:03:02,880 --> 00:03:06,250
Well, Grandpa will be disappointed, too.

70
00:03:06,250 --> 00:03:07,980
He loves Susan.

71
00:03:07,980 --> 00:03:11,300
She always reminds him of Grandma.

72
00:03:11,300 --> 00:03:13,850
Well, how's everything here?

73
00:03:13,850 --> 00:03:20,650
Fine. We were just wondering about this trunk.

74
00:03:20,650 --> 00:03:21,900
It's locked.

75
00:03:21,900 --> 00:03:24,900
Oh. I have the key. Grandpa sent it to me.
